login":"LostvayneOfChaos","node_id":"U_kgDOB1px4g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LostvayneOfChaos/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LostvayneOfChaos/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LostvayneOfChaos/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LostvayneOfChaos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LostvayneOfChaos/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LostvayneOfChaos","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Dolsoc/Imagenes_Medicas/commit/be380c78fc2fd4e3bdf485e95d6e4ad9a17081ba","node_id":"C_kwDOP8NbQdoAKGJlMzgwYzc4ZmMyZmQ0ZTNiZGY0ODVlOTVkNmU0YWQ5YTE3MDgxYmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Dolsoc/Imagenes_Medicas/commit/d0826fcb688ffc0822359053b027e70e2662b311","sha":"d0826fcb688ffc0822359053b027e70e2662b311","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Dolsoc/Imagenes_Medicas/commits/d0826fcb688ffc0822359053b027e70e2662b311"}],"sha":"be380c78fc2fd4e3bdf485e95d6e4ad9a17081ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Dolsoc/Imagenes_Medicas/commits/be380c78fc2fd4e3bdf485e95d6e4ad9a17081ba"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69012359?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Duvet05/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Duvet05/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Duvet05/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Duvet05/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Duvet05","id":69012359,"login":"Duvet05","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MDEyMzU5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Duvet05/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Duvet05/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Duvet05/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Duvet05/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Duvet05/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Duvet05","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Dolsoc/Imagenes_Medicas/commits/6c50dc61e01fe57b8a0a5cd513e086ffdd986d6f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-05T23:42:40Z","email":"69012359+Duvet05@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Gonzalo Galvez Cortez"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-05T23:42:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: avoid unsafe encounter datetime defaults (#450)\n\n* fix: avoid unsafe encounter datetime defaults\n\n* fix: scope vitest framework stubs to workspace libs only\n\nThe workspace framework stub aliases (@openmrs/esm-framework and its\n/src/internal entrypoint) were added to the shared base config used by\nboth defineWorkspaceVitestConfig and defineAppVitestConfig. Because\nmergeConfig concatenates base aliases first and Vite resolves aliases by\nfirst match, app tests started resolving @openmrs/esm-framework(/src/internal)\nto the lightweight lib stubs instead of @openmrs/esm-framework/mock and the\nreal internal stores. This broke esm-implementer-tools-app tests with\n''Maximum update depth exceeded'' loops in the implementer tools store.\n\nExtract a private defineBaseVitestConfig helper and pass workspaceBaseAliases\nonly for workspace/library configs. App configs pass no base framework\naliases, restoring their reliance on @openmrs/esm-framework/mock.\n\nCo-authored-by: Codesmith <codesmith-bot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: make workspace framework stubs opt-in per library\n\nThe previous fix routed all workspace libs through shared framework\nstub aliases, but only esm-form-engine-lib''s tests are written against\nthose stubs. The stubs shadow real @openmrs/esm-framework exports\n(parseDate, createUseStore, useStoreWithActions,\ngetDefaultsFromConfigSchema), breaking tests in esm-patient-common-lib\nand other libs that rely on the real package.\n\nGate the stub aliases behind an opt-in { frameworkStubs: true } option\nand enable it only for esm-form-engine-lib. All other workspace libs\nand apps resolve the real framework / mock, restoring green behavior.\n\nCo-authored-by: Codesmith <codesmith-bot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Codesmith <codesmith-bot@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"a4189643649ff9c21d67f772d61b5b6eea65125d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Dolsoc/Imagenes_Medicas/git/trees/a4189643649ff9c21d67f772d61b5b6eea65125d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Dolsoc/Imagenes_Medicas/git/commits/6c50dc61e01fe57b8a0a5cd513e086ffdd986d6f","verification":{"payload":"tree a4189643649ff9c21d67f772d61b5b6eea65125d\nparent 8f3003bbc2fdbf7268413c1e60b22fbe58d9182c\nauthor Gonzalo Galvez Cortez <69012359+Duvet05@users.noreply.github.com> 1783294960 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783294960 -0500\n\nfix: avoid unsafe encounter datetime defaults (#450)\n\n* fix: avoid unsafe encounter datetime defaults\n\n* fix: scope vitest framework stubs to workspace libs only\n\nThe workspace framework stub aliases (@openmrs/esm-framework and its\n/src/internal entrypoint) were added to the shared base config used by\nboth defineWorkspaceVitestConfig and defineAppVitestConfig. Because\nmergeConfig concatenates base aliases first and Vite resolves aliases by\nfirst match, app tests started resolving @openmrs/esm-framework(/src/internal)\nto the lightweight lib stubs instead of @openmrs/esm-framework/mock and the\nreal internal stores. This broke esm-implementer-tools-app tests with\n''Maximum update depth exceeded'' loops in the implementer tools store.\n\nExtract a private defineBaseVitestConfig helper and pass workspaceBaseAliases\nonly for workspace/library configs. App configs pass no base framework\naliases, restoring their reliance on @openmrs/esm-framework/mock.\n\nCo-authored-by: Codesmith <codesmith-bot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: make workspace framework stubs opt-in per library\n\nThe previous fix routed all workspace libs through shared framework\nstub aliases, but only esm-form-engine-lib''s tests are written against\nthose stubs. The stubs shadow real @openmrs/esm-framework exports\n(parseDate, createUseStore, useStoreWithActions,\ngetDefaultsFromConfigSchema), breaking tests in esm-patient-common-lib\nand other libs that rely on the real package.\n\nGate the stub aliases behind an opt-in { frameworkStubs: true } option\nand enable it only for esm-form-engine-lib. All other workspace libs\nand apps resolve the real framework / mock, restoring green behavior.\n\nCo-authored-by: Codesmith <codesmith-bot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Codesmith <codesmith-bot@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqSuvwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9VsQAJll/2Jwmt2ASoOoXoBZMrq8\nZU9xl5C1U4jIWMFqrlor/9dPKa3t+llPVm1C/yvoE944OgqA03YQQP393leVdP3w\nkFw4zBpE4aBgH+uC8OyxQBKCXUAqtAJUo7pegWVAxI9xxMDeYbgpTMuRpxYDWW3M\nggtKomuiwoG9MNWMVKU8dBLcifwX0N5H9+3nzg8DoeIO1qFA47BN/uzek5WtPqez\nrYqz0uyL9t9+sa6EGpbdSL4UvnLEjbImKnNqdWV8JEaundgM0UJfj2xfcXATJuqP\nVNNeDLll4sRChiVT7hwI+v7p16TgWIU6wSF22rb+nhsU3B6Bdqloj7PGWytL+WQ2\nfq10vJaC8N/oEIzg8jI3R3YLnUpUusz5BjflYlPyXoQF4HD4CxQepK5ZkBg8Ak7A\nuXvW2ehdfck8jy5r1paOfonZXQ+lK3sXJDb2uJ33GprgR94vUCXnFjB6NQPMJFoN\nANl6qzSbbLQ60dYesyNfXWQZ+9AeHWmQDApqIOHwDcMhcD1tTWgB1BqTDpxJS8Ze\nY9Y57CKOP3Uexn0hX3EY+sSeBHPKkMQCo8jNe2ouR8PqJ3m6zCZKVUVmr5T2An/9\ny0mSjN5LPCVFQ53nKa7Va5bdcr9y0EL1mLv6rNWE6NbVoCzSbAceqcSPeWtRBoLz\nWgQW0eMcXbsR7OnoxUKV\n=rz77\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-14T17:15:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-